l_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Co8pu98MLTJzsoRCYhau41", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the failing nightly build (tests/test_money.py::test_half_even).\n\n`src/money.py` documented banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, so `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` returned 2.67 instead of 2.66. This switches the quantize rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` says in its docstring that it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So `round_money(Decimal(\"2.665\"))` gave 2.67 when the test expects 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the import and the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't confirm the requirement itself: looking up FIN-212 in the advisory system returned \"unknown advisory,\" so I relied on the test and the docstring.", "type": "text"}]}]}